# The set of pipeline stages that must run for the M0 gate to mean anything.
#
# This file exists because CANONICAL_STAGES in test-m0.sh is the ONLY definition
# of what has to run, so deleting a stage from it removes the check and leaves
# no trace: the pipeline still runs, still reports green, and the summary simply
# has one fewer line. Verified: removing schema-hygiene from the list was silent.
#
# scripts/check-stage-manifest.sh asserts this manifest, the stage list, and the
# run_stage dispatch all agree. Three-way agreement means a stage cannot be
# dropped, added in one place only, or left with no implementation.
# `build` is here because the web app did not compile for several commits
# and no stage noticed: tsc and vitest both read tsconfig, and neither reads
# next.config.mjs or webpack's extension mapping. A check nobody runs is the
# same defect as a gate that checks nothing.
build
# `codegen-drift` is here for the same reason. The action-id union that makes
# `act('typo.id')` a compile error is generated from each feature's manifest and
# committed, so a feature can add an id, run nothing, and ship — and the
# type-level guarantee silently stops covering that feature while every other
# stage still reports green. It runs right after `build` because everything
# downstream (unit, integration, typecheck) reads the union it verifies.
codegen-drift
compose
migrations
seed
unit
integration
schema-drift
typecheck
architecture
schema-hygiene
removal-test
# The Moltbook check resolves every cited file:line against the checkout and
# fails on an uncited assertion of a claim the note records as dropped. It runs
# here because a check nobody invokes is the exact failure ba-risk-gates-e74
# exists to prevent, and this one was written to pass while enforcing nothing.
moltbook-claims
license
e2e-smoke
